# 2. USER ROLES AND ACCESS CONTROL

Implement these roles:

A. SUPER ADMIN
- Full platform access.
- Manage all registered shops.
- Activate, suspend and deactivate shops.
- View shop details and subscription status.
- Create and edit subscription plans.
- Configure plan limits and features.
- Approve or reject subscription payments.
- Manually assign subscriptions.
- Extend subscription expiry.
- View platform revenue and subscription analytics.
- Manage platform settings.
- View audit logs.
- Manage customer support requests.

B. SHOP OWNER
- Access only their own shop.
- Manage products, categories and inventory.
- Manage customers and orders.
- Manage suppliers and purchases.
- Manage POS billing if their plan allows it.
- Manage shop branding and online storefront.
- View reports according to subscription.
- Manage staff accounts and permissions.
- View and upgrade subscription.
- Manage their profile and shop settings.

C. SHOP STAFF
- Access only their assigned shop.
- Permissions controlled by shop owner.
- Support roles such as cashier, inventory manager and order manager.
- Restrict sensitive settings, subscription and financial permissions.
- Never access another shop's information.

D. PUBLIC CUSTOMER
- Browse public storefronts.
- Search products.
- Add products to cart.
- Place orders.
- Provide delivery information.
- View their own order information through secure access.
- Never access private shop or other customers' records.

Enforce role-based authorization on the backend and Firebase rules, not only in the frontend.

